The '''2019–20 Bundesliga''' was the 57th season of the [[Bundesliga]], Germany's premier [[Association football|football]] competition. It began on 16 August 2019, with seven-time defending champion Bayern Munich hosting Hertha BSC, and concluded on 27 June 2020.<ref>{{Cite news |date=7 December 2018 |title=DFB-Präsidium verabschiedet Rahmenterminkalender |language=|trans-title= |work=DFB.de |publisher=[[German Football Association]] |url=https://www.dfb.de/news/detail/dfb-praesidium-verabschiedet-rahmenterminkalender-196587/ |access-date=7 December 2018}}</ref><ref name="new dates" /> [[FC Bayern Munich|Bayern Munich]] were the seven-time defending champions, and won their record-extending 8th consecutive title and 30th title overall (29th in the Bundesliga era) on 16 June with two games to spare.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Johnston |first=Neil |date=16 June 2020 |title=Bayern Munich win eighth successive Bundesliga title after beating Werder Bremen |work=[[BBC Sport]] |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/53071043 |access-date=16 June 2020}}</ref> With 100 goals scored in 34 matches, Bayern became the second side to reach this milestone in a Bundesliga season, after the record 101 goals the club previously managed to score in [[1971–72 Bundesliga|1971–72]].<ref>{{Cite news |date=26 May 2020 |title=Die Rekorde der Bundesliga – historische Bestmarken im Überblick |language=de |trans-title=The Bundesliga records – historical benchmarks at a glance |work=[[Bundesliga]] |publisher=[[Deutsche Fußball Liga]] |url=https://www.bundesliga.com/de/bundesliga/news/rekorde-tore-meisterschaft-historie-bestmarken-spieler-meiste-3235 |access-date=30 May 2020}}</ref>

The number of substitutes allowed on the bench was increased from seven to nine for the 2019–20 season.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Reinold |first=Jan |date=11 April 2019 |title=Neue Regel: Mehr Auswechselspieler – auch Mehr-Kosten? |language=de |trans-title=New rule: More substitutes – also more costs? |work=[[Kicker (magazine)|Kicker]] |publisher=[[Kicker (sports magazine)|kicker-sportmagazin]] |url=https://www.kicker.de/neue-regel_mehr-auswechselspieler---auch-mehr-kosten-746692/artikel |access-date=26 July 2019}}</ref>

On 13 March 2020, the [[Deutsche Fußball Liga|DFL]] suspended the Bundesliga and [[2019–20 2. Bundesliga|2. Bundesliga]] due to the [[COVID-19 pandemic in Germany|COVID-19 pandemic]].<ref name="postponed" /> After consultation with the German government, the league resumed [[Behind closed doors (sport)|behind closed doors]] on 16 May 2020.<ref>{{Cite news |date=6 May 2020 |title=Politik ermöglicht Saisonfortsetzung ab der zweiten Maihälfte |work=dfb.de |url=https://www.dfb.de/news/detail/politik-ermoeglicht-saisonfortsetzung-ab-der-zweiten-maihaelfte-215328/ |access-date=6 May 2020}}</ref> Due to the postponement, the final matchday on 27 June was the second latest date any Bundesliga season has concluded, after the [[1971–72 Bundesliga|1971–72 season]] (which concluded a day later).<ref name="Der Spiegel">{{Cite news |last=Thilo |first=Adam |date=12 June 2020 |title=Welche Entscheidungen jetzt schon fallen können |language=de |trans-title=Which decisions can now already be made |work=[[Der Spiegel (website)|Der Spiegel]] |url=https://www.spiegel.de/sport/fussball/fussball-bundesliga-welche-entscheidungen-jetzt-schon-fallen-koennen-a-495d5e58-cb1f-4173-bb2d-f3ee048b1771 |access-date=13 June 2020}}</ref>

==Effects of the COVID-19 pandemic==
Due to the [[COVID-19 pandemic in Germany]], on 8 March 2020 the [[Federal Ministry of Health (Germany)|Federal Minister of Health]], [[Jens Spahn]] recommended cancelling events with more than 1,000 people.<ref>{{Cite news |date=9 March 2020 |title=Bundesliga bald vor leeren Rängen? |language=de |trans-title=Bundesliga soon before empty seats? |work=[[ARD (broadcaster)|ARD]] |url=https://www.tagesschau.de/inland/corona-bundesliga-101.html |access-date=10 March 2020}}</ref> The following day, the [[Deutsche Fußball Liga|DFL]] announced that the Bundesliga season would be completed to ensure planning for the following season, and that any postponements would be to matchdays en bloc.<ref>{{Cite news |date=9 March 2020 |title=DFL-Präsidium befasst sich mit Corona-Virus: Ansetzungstermine für den kommenden Spieltag bleiben unverändert |language=de |trans-title=DFL Executive Committee deals with coronavirus: Scheduling dates for the coming matchday remain unchanged |work=[[Deutsche Fußball Liga]] |url=https://www.dfl.de/de/aktuelles/dfl-praesidium-befasst-sich-mit-corona-virus-ansetzungstermine-fuer-den-kommenden-spieltag-bleiben-unveraendert/ |access-date=10 March 2020}}</ref> On 10 March, it was announced that the catch-up match between [[Borussia Mönchengladbach]] and [[1. FC Köln]] on 11 March would be played [[Behind closed doors (sport)|behind closed doors]], the first such occurrence in league history.<ref>{{Cite news |date=10 March 2020 |title=Erstes Bundesliga-Geisterspiel: Gladbach gegen Köln ohne Zuschauer |language=de |trans-title=First Bundesliga match behind closed doors: Gladbach against Köln without spectators |work=[[Kicker (sports magazine)|kicker]] |url=https://www.kicker.de/erstes_bundesliga_geisterspiel_gladbach_gegen_koeln_ohne_zuschauer-771857/artikel |access-date=10 March 2020}}</ref> All fixtures on matchday 26 (13–16 March) were planned to be played without spectators due to local restrictions on public gatherings,<ref>{{Cite news |date=12 March 2020 |title=Geisterspieltag, Revierderby und Herrlich-Debüt |language=de |trans-title=Matchday behind closed doors, Revierderby and Herrlich debut |work=[[Kicker (sports magazine)|kicker]] |url=https://www.kicker.de/geisterspieltag_revierderby_und_herrlich_debuet-771944/artikel |access-date=13 March 2020}}</ref> but the round was subsequently postponed on 13 March due to safety issues.<ref name="postponed">{{Cite news |date=13 March 2020 |title=Nach aktuellen Entwicklungen in Zusammenhang mit dem Corona-Virus: DFL beschließt Verlegung des 26. Spieltags der Bundesliga und 2. Bundesliga |language=de |trans-title=After current developments in connection with the coronavirus: DFL decides to postpone the 26th matchday of the Bundesliga and 2. Bundesliga |work=[[Deutsche Fußball Liga]] |url=https://www.dfl.de/de/aktuelles/nach-aktuellen-entwicklungen-in-zusammenhang-mit-dem-corona-virus-dfl-beschliesst-verlegung-des-26-spieltags-der-bundesliga-und-2-bundesliga/ |access-date=13 March 2020}}</ref> On 16 March, the DFL General Assembly suspended the league until at least 2 April, and scheduled another meeting for the last week of March to discuss how the competition should proceed.<ref>{{Cite news |date=16 March 2020 |title=DFL-Mitgliederversammlung beschließt weitere Verlegung für die Bundesliga und 2. Bundesliga – Erneutes Club-Treffen in der letzten März-Woche vereinbart |language=de |trans-title=DFL General Assembly approves further postponement of the Bundesliga and 2. Bundesliga – another club meeting agreed upon for the last week of March |work=[[Deutsche Fußball Liga]] |url=https://www.dfl.de/de/aktuelles/dfl-mitgliederversammlung-beschliesst-weitere-verlegung-fuer-die-bundesliga-und-2-bundesliga-erneutes-club-treffen-in-der-letzten-maerz-woche-vereinbart/ |access-date=16 March 2020}}</ref> The DFL General Assembly, at their meeting on 31 March, chose to extend the suspension until at least 30 April per the recommendation of the executive committee.<ref>{{Cite news |date=24 March 2020 |title=DFL-Präsidium empfiehlt Aussetzung von Bundesliga und 2. Bundesliga bis mindestens 30. April – Medienrechte-Ausschreibung wird verschoben |language=de |trans-title=DFL Executive Committee recommends suspension of Bundesliga and 2. Bundesliga until at least 30 April – Media rights tendering to be postponed |work=[[Deutsche Fußball Liga]] |url=https://www.dfl.de/de/aktuelles/dfl-praesidium-empfiehlt-aussetzung-von-bundesliga-und-2-bundesliga-bis-mindestens-30-april-medienrechte-ausschreibung-wird-verschoben/ |access-date=24 March 2020}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |date=31 March 2020 |title=Mitgliederversammlung der DFL beschließt weitreichende Anpassungen im Lizenzierungsverfahren zur Entlastung von Clubs |language=de |trans-title=DFL general meeting decides on far-reaching adjustments to the licensing procedure to ease the burden on clubs |work=[[Deutsche Fußball Liga]] |url=https://www.dfl.de/de/aktuelles/dfl-mv-31-03-2020/ |access-date=6 May 2020}}</ref> At the meeting, the DFL established a sports medicine and special match operations task force responsible for examining a safe method to resume league play.<ref>{{Cite news |date=1 May 2020 |title=Konzept der "Task Force Sportmedizin / Sonderspielbetrieb" |language=de |trans-title=Concept of the "Task Force Sports Medicine/Special Match Operations |work=[[Deutsche Fußball Liga]] |url=https://www.dfl.de/de/hintergrund/spielplanung/task-force-konzept/ |access-date=6 May 2020}}</ref>

On 13 March 2020, [[Luca Kilian]] of [[SC Paderborn 07|SC Paderborn]] was the first Bundesliga player to test positive for [[COVID-19]].<ref>{{Cite news |date=13 March 2020 |title=Erste Erkrankung |language=de |trans-title=First illness |work=[[SC Paderborn 07]] |url=https://www.scp07.de/Newsarchiv/Erste-Erkrankung.html |access-date=14 March 2020}}</ref> By 21 March 2020, several clubs, including [[Eintracht Frankfurt]] and [[Hertha BSC]], were under quarantine after multiple players and staff had tested positive, and training was made impossible for most others by curfews or the closure of facilities.<ref name="sport1_21Mar">{{Cite web |date=21 March 2020 |title=DFL wird längere Pause beschließen |trans-title=DFL will decide on a longer break |url=https://www.sport1.de/fussball/bundesliga/2020/03/bundesliga-dfl-beraet-am-kommenden-dienstag-ueber-weitere-aussetzung-der-spiele |website=sport1.de |language=de}}</ref> The DFL looked into possible scenarios to finish the season regularly.<ref name="sport1_21Mar" /> However, several virologists raised doubts, stating that any professional football matches in Germany, including those behind closed doors, were unrealistic for at least the next 12 months.<ref>{{Cite web |date=19 March 2020 |title=Virologe: Kein Profifußball mehr in diesem Jahr |trans-title=Virologist: No more professional football this year |url=https://www.ndr.de/sport/fussball/Virologe-Kein-Profifussball-mehr-in-diesem-Jahr,schmidtchanasit106.html |website=NDR |language=de |access-date=21 March 2020 |archive-date=7 November 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201107040510/https://www.ndr.de/sport/fussball/Virologe-Kein-Profifussball-mehr-in-diesem-Jahr,schmidtchanasit106.html |url-status=dead }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=21 March 2020 |title=Virologen schlagen Alarm: Schlechte Aussichten für Fußballfans |trans-title=Virologists raise alarm: Bad news for football fans |url=https://www.t-online.de/sport/id_87567436/coronavirus-pause-schlechte-aussichten-fuer-bundesliga-fans.html |website=t-online.de |language=de}}</ref> In his report for the 31 March DFL meeting, virologist [[Alexander Kekulé]] recommended to write off the current season.<ref name="Kekule1">{{Cite web |date=31 March 2020 |title=Bundesliga beschäftigt sich mit radikaleren Alternativen |trans-title=Bundesliga is looking at more radical alternatives |url=https://www.welt.de/sport/article206912997/Corona-Bundesliga-beschaeftigt-sich-mit-radikaleren-Alternativen.html |access-date=4 April 2020 |website=Die Welt |language=de}}</ref> On 4 April 2020, he clarified that matches behind closed doors were possible in principle, but would require extensive measures, including a total of about 20,000 tests for COVID-19 for the players and staff (testing every player before the start of each game), and an extended quarantine for everyone involved. Kekulé was doubtful though that those measures could be justified at a time when tests for the general population were in short supply.<ref name="Kekule2">{{Cite web |date=4 April 2020 |title=Arzt Kekulé zu Bundesliga-Geisterspielen: "Rein virologisch wäre es lösbar" |trans-title=Virologist Kekulé on Bundesliga phantom matches: "From a virological standpoint, it is possible" |url=https://www.kicker.de/arzt_kekul_zu_bundesliga_geisterspielen_rein_virologisch_waere_es_loesbar_-773436/artikel |access-date=4 April 2020 |website=Kicker |language=de}}</ref><ref name="Kekule1" />

On 3 April 2020, the DFL reported that the financial situation of most teams was more serious than thought. Of the 36 professional football clubs in the Bundesliga and [[2. Bundesliga]], 13 would have to declare bankruptcy by May or June unless league operations resumed by then, including four teams from the Bundesliga. Twelve of those clubs had already used the outstanding license fees (which are dependent on the season to be continued) to pay their March debts to creditors.<ref>{{Cite web |date=3 April 2020 |title=13 der 36 Profiklubs droht Insolvenz – noch in dieser Saison |trans-title=13 of the 36 professional clubs threatened by bankruptcy before season is over |url=https://www.kicker.de/13_der_36_profiklubs_droht_insolvenz_noch_in_dieser_saison-773385/artikel |website=Kicker |language=de}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=3 April 2020 |title=Bundesligist droht Insolvenz |trans-title=Bundesliga clubs threatened by bankruptcy |url=https://www.sport.de/news/ne4013179/live-blog-zur-corona-krise-vier-bundesliga-klubs-droht-insolvenz---klubs-zurueck-im-training/ |website=sport.de |language=de}}</ref> At their 31 March meeting, the DFL had decided that clubs that enter [[Insolvency#Germany|insolvency proceedings]] this season would not suffer the usual deduction of points, and clubs that enter proceedings next season only lose three instead of the usual nine points.<ref>{{Cite web |date=31 March 2020 |title=Punktabzüge und Liquidität: DFL passt Lizenzierung an |trans-title=Point deductions and liquidity: DFL adjusts licensing regulations |url=https://www.kicker.de/punktabzuege_und_liquiditaet_dfl_passt_lizenzierung_an-773139/artikel |website=Kicker |language=de}}</ref>

By 23 April 2020, the DFL had targeted 9 May as a possible resumption date for the Bundesliga.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Eckner |first=Constantin |date=23 April 2020 |title=Bundesliga 'ready to return on 9 May', says German Football League |work=[[BBC Sport]] |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/52379825 |access-date=24 April 2020}}</ref> However, this goal suffered a setback when [[1. FC Köln]] announced on 1 May that three people at the club tested positive, without showing any symptoms.<ref>{{Cite news |date=1 May 2020 |title=Ergebnisse der Tests auf COVID-19 |language=de |trans-title=Results of the tests for COVID-19 |work=[[1. FC Köln]] |url=https://fc.de/fc-info/news/detailseite/details/ergebnisse-der-tests-auf-covid-19/ |access-date=6 May 2020 |archive-date=7 November 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201107040557/https://fc.de/fc-info/news/detailseite/details/ergebnisse-der-tests-auf-covid-19/ |url-status=dead }}</ref> This was done as part of a wave of 1,724 tests carried out involving personnel of the 36 Bundesliga and 2. Bundesliga clubs, in coordination with the [[Federal Ministry of Labour and Social Affairs]], which resulted in seven further positive results in addition to those of Köln.<ref>{{Cite news |date=4 May 2020 |title=Rund 1.700 Corona-Tests bei allen 36 Clubs der Bundesliga und 2. Bundesliga vor dem Start des Mannschaftstrainings erfolgt |language=de |trans-title=Around 1,700 corona tests at all 36 clubs in the Bundesliga and 2. Bundesliga before the start of team training |work=[[Deutsche Fußball Liga]] |url=https://www.dfl.de/de/aktuelles/rund-1-700-corona-tests-bei-allen-36-clubs-der-bundesliga-und-2-bundesliga-vor-dem-start-des-mannschaftstrainings-erfolgt/ |access-date=6 May 2020}}</ref> After consultation with the German government, chancellor [[Angela Merkel]] and the [[Minister president (Germany)|leaders of the states of Germany]] approved the resumption of the leagues for the second half of May, with matches behind closed doors.<ref>{{Cite news |date=6 May 2020 |title=Politik ermöglicht Saison-Fortsetzung ab der zweiten Mai-Hälfte – Statement von Christian Seifert |language=de |trans-title=Policy allows season to continue from the second half of May – statement by Christian Seifert |work=[[Deutsche Fußball Liga]] |url=https://www.dfl.de/de/aktuelles/politik-ermoeglicht-saison-fortsetzung-ab-der-zweiten-mai-haelfte-statement-von-christian-seifert/ |access-date=6 May 2020}}</ref><ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Straus |first=Brian |date=6 May 2020 |title=Germany's Bundesliga Gets the Green Light to Return This Month |magazine=[[Sports Illustrated]] |url=https://www.si.com/soccer/2020/05/06/bundesliga-return-approval-germany-government-dfl-coronavirus |access-date=6 May 2020}}</ref> The following day, the DFL confirmed that the Bundesliga would resume on 16 May, a Saturday, with matchday 26.<ref>{{Cite news |date=7 May 2020 |title=Re-Start ohne Freitagsspiel: Bundesliga geht erst am 16. Mai weiter |language=de |trans-title=Restart without Friday matches: Bundesliga continues on 16 May |work=kicker |url=https://www.kicker.de/re_start_ohne_freitagsspiel_bundesliga_geht_erst_am_16_mai_weiter-775139/artikel |access-date=7 May 2020}}</ref> The final matchday of the season (round 34), originally scheduled for 16 May, took place on 27 June,<ref name="new dates">{{Cite news |date=7 May 2020 |title=Saison-Fortsetzung am 16. Mai – Rückkehr von Bundesliga und 2. Bundesliga startet mit dem 26. Spieltag |language=de |trans-title=Season continues on 16 May – return of Bundesliga and 2. Bundesliga begins with matchday 26 |work=[[Deutsche Fußball Liga]] |url=https://www.dfl.de/de/aktuelles/saison-fortsetzung-am-16-mai-rueckkehr-von-bundesliga-und-2-bundesliga-startet-mit-dem-26-spieltag/ |access-date=7 May 2020}}</ref> making it the second latest date any Bundesliga season has concluded. Only the [[1971–72 Bundesliga|1971–72 season]] finished later (due to [[UEFA Euro 1972]]), concluding on 28 June.<ref name="Der Spiegel" />

The relegation play-offs between [[SV Werder Bremen|Werder Bremen]], the 16th-placed team of the Bundesliga, and the 3rd-placed team of the [[2019–20 2. Bundesliga|2. Bundesliga]] take place as planned. Per the competition regulations, clubs in the Bundesliga and 2. Bundesliga were required to compete in all matches following the restart, even if some players test positive, provided the team has enough healthy players available.<ref>{{Cite news |date=7 May 2020 |title=Das alles hat die DFL entschieden |language=de |trans-title=Here is everything the DFL has decided |work=kicker |url=https://www.kicker.de/das_alles_hat_die_dfl_entschieden-775140/artikel |access-date=9 May 2020}}</ref> On 14 May, after a meeting of all clubs, five substitutions were permitted, which has been temporarily allowed by [[International Football Association Board|IFAB]] following a proposal by [[FIFA]] to lessen the impact of fixture congestion.<ref>{{Cite news |date=27 April 2020 |title=Fifa proposes use of five substitutions to help with fixture congestion |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/52443195 |access-date=7 May 2020}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |date=8 May 2020 |title=Five substitutes option temporarily allowed for competition organisers |work=[[International Football Association Board]] |url=https://www.theifab.com/news/five-substitutes-option-temporarily-allowed-for-competition-organisers |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210514050706/https://theifab.com/news/five-substitutes-option-temporarily-allowed-for-competition-organisers |url-status=dead |archive-date=14 May 2021 |access-date=9 May 2020 }}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |date=14 May 2020 |title=DFL: Saison notfalls im Juli zu Ende spielen |work=dfb.de |url=https://www.dfb.de/news/detail/dfl-saison-notfalls-im-juli-zu-ende-spielen-215549/ |access-date=14 May 2020}}</ref> The broadcaster [[Sky Sport (Germany)|Sky Sport]] announced that for the first two weeks after the restart, the Bundesliga and 2. Bundesliga simulcast ("conference") would be shown on [[free-to-air]] television in Germany, in order to prevent gatherings of people without [[Pay television|pay TV]] subscriptions.<ref>{{Cite news |date=7 May 2020 |title=Die 1. und 2. Bundesliga kommen teilweise ins Free-TV |language=de |trans-title=The 1. and 2. Bundesliga come partly on free TV |work=kicker |url=https://www.kicker.de/die_1_und_2_bundesliga_kommen_teilweise_ins_free_tv-775011/artikel |access-date=9 May 2020}}</ref>

