Following a victory against [[VfB Stuttgart]] on away goals in the [[2018–19 Bundesliga#Relegation play-offs|relegation/promotion play-offs]], [[1. FC Union Berlin|Union Berlin]] were promoted to the Bundesliga for the first time in their history, becoming the [[List of clubs in the Bundesliga|56th club to feature in the Bundesliga]], and the first from the former [[East Berlin]].<ref>{{cite web |title=Union vs. Hertha: why is the Berlin derby such a special fixture? |url=https://www.bundesliga.com/en/bundesliga/news/union-hertha-why-is-the-berlin-derby-such-a-special-fixture-wall-7822 |website=Bundesliga |access-date=29 July 2020}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |date=27 May 2019 |title=0:0 in Berlin! Union steigt auf, der VfB ab |language=de |trans-title=0–0 in Berlin! Union rises, VfB relegated |work=[[Kicker (magazine)|Kicker]] |publisher=[[Kicker (sports magazine)|kicker-sportmagazin]] |url=https://www.kicker.de/union-gegen-stuttgart-2019-bundesliga-relegation-4552769/analyse |access-date=28 May 2019}}</ref>

